# Mosaic Notes synthetic repository

Owner: Synthetic fixture maintainer. This project holds example documentation
only; no application, database, credentials, or production data exists.
Use synthetic content and respect higher-priority instructions and permissions.
Guidance grants no new authority. Preserve unrelated work and existing approval.

Before working in a subtree, inspect applicable ancestor-to-target guidance,
including overrides and deeper files. Repeat for each target area. Apply local
rules only to their files; a directory change does not reload startup guidance.
Report unresolved conflicts and continue unaffected work.

The default documentation convention is sentence case. UI and backend rules
are distinct; deeper backend guidance may explicitly specialize entity wording.
Every external-facing report must include its scope. Local files may not waive
this shared requirement without owner resolution of the conflict.

Review Markdown and relative links per [the fixture guide](README.md). There is
no application startup/build or stack test. Follow that guide for reviewed Git
updates and rollback; verify restored guidance in fresh tasks.
